      note: "MISO keeper — and the CONFIRMED root cause of its C7 COAL_PRB cycling failure (pins ~55% of each regulated plant at VOM in all 8760h). miso-102 PROVED the attribution by A/B on the current keeper and closed the surrounding lane space. Removing it (sunk_fixed) REJECTED AGAIN, now for a STRUCTURAL reason rather than a gate one: cv_ratio 0.467->0.727 / 0.476->0.931 (FAIL->PASS) but 2025 stays 0.364, C1 goes PASS->FAIL (16/16 -> 11/16), and COAL_BIT OVERSHOOTS to 2.6-2.8x measured off-peak variability — the arm deletes regulated self-commitment (SOM Table 7, 53-56% of coal starts) along with the category error, so rule 1 forbids promoting it just as it forbids rejecting a correct mechanism on gates. PRE-REGISTERED AS A NON-KEEPER BEFORE THE SOLVE. Diagnosis (committed artifacts, no solve) refutes FIVE alternatives: no floor (D-2 reliability_floor 0.19-0.35% of class energy), no mix effect (0 plants dropped from the D-1 pairing), not the benchmark basis, NOT the miso-101 §5 cancellation (off-peak coherence 0.92-0.98 on BOTH sides; phase matches, only amplitude misses), and SEPARABLE from miso-89 (all-season, worst in winter/shoulder, h0-h14 vs miso-89's summer HE16-18). 100% of byte-flat PRB plants are regulated (44-50% of class energy); the model INVERTS the measured within-day flexibility ordering (actual regulated 0.197 vs merchant 0.134; model 0.073 vs 0.351). NO OFFER-STEEPENING LEVER IS ADMISSIBLE: the model's coal is already 0.9-2.8x the real fleet's price-responsiveness. PRICE FORMATION IS NOT THE ROUTE (miso-102 P5 FALSIFIED IN DIRECTION): the arm fixes the dispatch wave while NARROWING the off-peak price-CV ratio (0.460->0.377, 0.530->0.418, 0.331->0.311) and pushing the night price further from the meter — so C7 and the diurnal-spread compression are SEPARATE misses and must not be pursued as one. Named successor lane (minimum-take LP constraint over the contract period, priced by its dual) is now ADJUDICATED DATA-BLOCKED by miso-103, ex ante, NO LP BUILT: the only forward-regenerable tonnage candidate — contract_share x lagged/trailing-mean Schedule-5 receipts — FAILS the chartered pin-strength test. Log-space cross-section R2 vs same-year burn 0.87-0.94 with lag-1/lag-3/lag-5 all equivalent (receipts autocorrelation IS the contract persistence, so lagging is cosmetic de-identification of the same answer key); floor = 0.96/1.14/0.98x same-year actual tonnage aggregate, dictating 90-96% of the 39 regulated target plants' actual CAMPD coal energy; and it BINDS (vs the discount-free miso-102 arm B: 22/33/20 of 38 plants, 32/44/20 TWh forced above unconstrained economics) — so the constraint, not economics, would write annual coal energy ~= actuals (rule 13 pin, worse than miso-96 §7's ~85% same-year case). 2024 overshoots outright (floor 1.136x actual burn, >=100% at 77% of plants — a hard >= floor forces MORE coal than reality; softening it needs a fitted penalty price, rule 24). Delta test R2 0.17: the trailing mean carries the LEVEL of the outcome without the year-specific driver signal — the exact inversion of rule 13 admissibility. DO NOT REDO with any receipts-derived tonnage variant (window/lag/smoothing/scalar shrink — all the same answer key or a residual-fitted knob). UNBLOCK requires genuinely contractual ex-ante data. miso-104 RAN THAT SOURCING PASS (no LP, no intake) and OPENED THE STANDING ASK docs/handoffs/miso-coal-contract-tonnage-data-ask-2026-07.md — the second MISO data ask beside outage grain. Result: the datum EXISTS as a form field and as a published document class, but NO source carries it at plant grain across the 39-plant / 26-owner / 12-state target set for 2023-2025, so NO candidate reached the threshold of being a testable series and the pin-strength battery could not be run on anything. (a) FERC Form 580 (docket IN79-6) Q6a collects a genuinely ex-ante 'Fuel quantity - Coal (x10^3 tons)' PER CONTRACT with signing + expiration dates, and Q6b links deliveries to a named Destination Plant — but it fails on FOUR measured blockers: the quantity is CONTRACT grain while the plant is only on the DELIVERY rows (pushing it to plant grain needs delivered-ton weights = the refuted answer key, so only 1:1 contract-plant cases are admissible and that share is UNMEASURED); Q6 is answered only by holders of a WHOLESALE 18 CFR 35.14 FAC, estimated at 24 respondents NATIONALLY across all fuels/regions (ICR IC25-1-000, 2024-12-03) while the MISO set recovers fuel through STATE retail clauses; scope is contracts >1 year only; and the biennial vintage means the latest filed form (2024) covers CY2022-2023 only — CY2024-2025 arrives with the 2026 form, DUE 2026-10-30, so today it spans ONE of three training years (rule 16). No bulk/API access (eLibrary Cloudflare-gated SPA; /eLibraryAPI probes 404). (b) State fuel-clause filings: KENTUCKY is the exemplar of the right datum and is PUBLIC and UN-REDACTED (807 KAR 5:056 — the Alliance/LG&E-KU J24007 agreement publishes a Base Quantity TABLE by delivery year 2024-2028 with quarterly nomination minimums, make-up tons and force majeure) but covers ONE MISO plant, D B Wilson = 1.5/1.1/1.1 % of target tonnage, an order of magnitude under the ask's coverage bar, and its index is a rolling recent-filings view not an archive. The LARGE MISO states file it under seal: Indiana's public FAC exhibit section 'VI. Coal Contracts and Inventory' is purely qualitative with contract specifics in confidential attachments (Cause 38702 FAC-91, 2023-09-05). MICHIGAN PSCR (MCL 460.6j — genuinely ex-ante plan-year filing, DTE+Consumers = 12.8 % of 2025 tonnage) is the ONE remaining unchecked state lead. (c) IRP fuel-budget exhibits REJECTED ON KIND, do not re-attempt: IRPs publish MODELLED burn, i.e. another model's forecast of the outcome — rule 13's forbidden half in a worse form than receipts. Also ruled out permanently: EIA-923 Schedule 2 purchase-type/expiration-date subsetting (the dates are terms but the quantity is a delivery), SEC 10-K purchase obligations (company grain, DOLLARS), coal-producer 'committed and priced tons' (producer grain, no plant key), FERC Form 1 p.402 (burn, ex post), STB waybill (ex-post, no plant id). The ask sets a coverage bar (>=15 of 39 plants AND >=60 % of tonnage in EVERY training year) and makes the pin-strength battery BINDING with explicit thresholds — level-R2 >=0.80 FAILS, no year may put the aggregate floor above actual burn, and the DELTA test is the one that must PASS: an admissible contractual series shows the INVERSE profile of the receipts construction (lower level-R2, higher delta-R2 than miso-103's 0.87-0.94 / 0.172). Bounded next experiment (ask §8): pull the 2024 Form 580 filings for the 26 target owners and count 1:1 contract-plant coal contracts covering 2023 — if it clears, the lane is TIMING-blocked (unblocks when the 2026 form lands CY2024-25) rather than data-blocked. C7 COAL_PRB therefore stands failing 3/3 on the keeper with NO open admissible lever, and its continuation is a data ask, not a solve.",
