      cells: "UUUKUU",
      note: "Replaces eGRID's STEAM-CREDITED PLHTRT for topping-cycle cogens with (PLHTIAN + CHPCHTI)/PLNGENAN — eGRID's own published CHP useful-thermal heat-input allocation added back on the same NET denominator, so no gross-to-net factor is involved (that is what blocked the CEMS route, FINDING-miso98 §6.1). Validated against independently metered CAMPD heat input at 1.00000 on 19/22 covered MISO plants. Zero fitted parameters; scoped to CC_CHP/CT_CHP on turbine physics (a boiler-first back-pressure cogen's fuel is process fuel). MISO KEEPER (miso-99: 72 generators / 6,732 MW repriced; C3a better in all three years vs a same-HEAD flag-off control, no criterion regressed, C3b kill guard held). Untested elsewhere — caiso-128 §3 measures CHP understated 12-62 % in five ISOs and OVER-corrected +40 % in CAISO by the hand factor this supersedes, so every ISO is a transfer candidate (rule 25: each derives its own artifact).",
