      note: "CAISO+NEISO+MISO keeper. PJM: rule-24 own-fleet validation REFUTED the slopes on PJM CAMPD (pjm-95 demotion). MISO KEEPER via the miso-101 hour-grain leg — temp_derate_hourly_grain feeds the curve an hourly dry-bulb reconstructed from daily TMIN/TMAX instead of the day-flat TMAX that carries zero hour-of-day signal; temp_derate_mean_anchored drops the onset hinge and anchors on the zone annual mean so the arm is a level-neutral SHAPE overlay; temp_derate_classes scopes it (MISO: ST_CHP+CT_CHP only); temp_derate_slope_st_chp / temp_derate_slope_ct_chp carry MISO's OWN measured slope 0.00141/C (derive_campd_temp_derate_params.py, 6 CEMS-identifiable cogens 2023-25, cap-weighted p50, LOO-stable 0.00130-0.00153) — ~5x below the committed literature CC slope, MISO's own confirmation of pjm-95 non-transferability. Onset scan finds NO 15 C hinge (response measured at 0.0036/0.0030 per C in the 5-10/10-15 C bins). Result: Beaumont's floored slice goes byte-flat -> r +0.964/+0.958/+0.984 vs its own CEMS meter, trough h15 = meter trough, all 4 pre-registered gates pass. Distinct from gt_ambient_derate, measured inert in MISO (miso-90). ERCOT/NYISO untested (NYISO keeper sets it explicitly false).",
